                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0e0f3e3-6a4f-3f53-99fa-a6a0a2e20a1d",
                        "entry_id": "b97393b5-6b25-377e-8f7b-d70461f0cbc3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "геол. вулканическое стекло — стекловатая вулканическая горная порода (красная, чёрная, серая, иногда с красивым отливом) с раковистым, режущим изломом, образующаяся при застывании вязкой кислой лавы"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b8ab197-b7d5-49be-b544-00726f69cf9f",
                                "sense_id": "d0e0f3e3-6a4f-3f53-99fa-a6a0a2e20a1d",
                                "text": "В долине Дуйки Поляков нашел ножеобразный осколок обсидиана, наконечники стрел из камня, точильные камни, каменные топоры и проч."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "07c02a26-a336-4434-88dd-3e02a92caa87",
                        "source_entry_id": "b97393b5-6b25-377e-8f7b-d70461f0cbc3",
                        "source_sense_id": "d0e0f3e3-6a4f-3f53-99fa-a6a0a2e20a1d",
                        "target_lang_word": "obsidian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "obsidian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b354bfa-113d-34bc-842f-6c0272318433",
                                        "entry_id": "20e34694-bdaf-307e-828b-beb45519d743",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of naturally occurring black glass produced by volcanoes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6de35b8c-ea45-4313-9fe1-c29b1d056b4c",
                                                "sense_id": "7b354bfa-113d-34bc-842f-6c0272318433",
                                                "text": "The Neolithic culture from 8000 to 6000 B.C., however, was a brilliant period of the revival of crafts, the transformation of gathering into gardening, the growth of a cross-cultural obsidian trade, and the rise of towns."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e3dcfb57-9837-33dd-a17d-a6a6589b07a4",
                                        "entry_id": "20e34694-bdaf-307e-828b-beb45519d743",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A slightly bluish black, the color of obsidian glass."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "obsidian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1839bf0b-ecba-342a-8b55-485384a38aac",
                                        "entry_id": "5a55444c-df8e-3e29-9fed-df74658da530",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Black."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "poetic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7069424e-0ea1-4db3-8785-d0ed4daa6d74",
                                                "sense_id": "1839bf0b-ecba-342a-8b55-485384a38aac",
                                                "text": "Looks like a yellow biscuit of a buttery cue ball moon / Rolling maverick across an obsidian sky"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "42441cf7-3f1b-4d80-9c43-0856d0dcca73",
                        "source_entry_id": "b97393b5-6b25-377e-8f7b-d70461f0cbc3",
                        "source_sense_id": "d0e0f3e3-6a4f-3f53-99fa-a6a0a2e20a1d",
                        "target_lang_word": "obsidiana",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "obsidiana",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e518d1e-b814-388b-b69c-c45e63f23048",
                                        "entry_id": "95ccb21d-a4c5-3be6-af1f-7000f08871d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mineral de origen volcánico vítreo y compacto de color verde muy oscuro o negro, usado antiguamente por los pueblos amerindios en la fabricación de armas cortantes, flechas y adornos"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Minerales"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "213762fc-4b05-49a6-a60a-d628073f4de5",
                        "source_entry_id": "b97393b5-6b25-377e-8f7b-d70461f0cbc3",
                        "source_sense_id": "d0e0f3e3-6a4f-3f53-99fa-a6a0a2e20a1d",
                        "target_lang_word": "Obsidian",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Obsidian",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7862a1a1-99b9-3ab3-bfde-0817957d5376",
                                        "entry_id": "25a8c896-9e16-3660-99c4-129411978662",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "dunkles und glasiges Gestein vulkanischer Herkunft"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b090368-8f46-44da-ac1e-6259e2d14e3f",
                                                "sense_id": "7862a1a1-99b9-3ab3-bfde-0817957d5376",
                                                "text": "„Steinwerkzeuge aus Obsidian und Flint lassen sich unter bestimmten Voraussetzungen aufgrund ihrer Patinaschichten, deren Stärke temperatur- und zeitabhängig ist, datieren.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16f95e55-4249-435c-bc1e-37e48fba3545",
                                                "sense_id": "7862a1a1-99b9-3ab3-bfde-0817957d5376",
                                                "text": "„Obsidian […] tritt in allen Fundstellen als Schneidewerkzeug, Pfeil- und Speerspitzen auf.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "904fd928-4fd1-4be7-8767-c7734b0d517b",
                                                "sense_id": "7862a1a1-99b9-3ab3-bfde-0817957d5376",
                                                "text": "„Die nötigen Mittel konnten durch den Handel mit Obsidian gewonnen werden, der von allen Völkern für Messer oder Waffen erforderlich war, denn das vulkanische Glas hatte messerscharfe Kanten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f52008f-6959-412b-b905-7d8625641064",
                                                "sense_id": "7862a1a1-99b9-3ab3-bfde-0817957d5376",
                                                "text": "„Der Boden war von plutonischen Kräften geformt, auf Schritt und Tritt traf man auf Basaltbrocken, Bimsstein, erratische Blöcke und Obsidiane.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2b4eef3b-a810-4e4c-b978-2902d9560eb1",
                        "source_entry_id": "b97393b5-6b25-377e-8f7b-d70461f0cbc3",
                        "source_sense_id": "d0e0f3e3-6a4f-3f53-99fa-a6a0a2e20a1d",
                        "target_lang_word": "obsidienne",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "obsidienne",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b35b669-d90b-3940-a7a9-21ae09525594",
                                        "entry_id": "fe786349-e6b8-3f65-aa6b-20276b9d9e3c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Roche éruptive à structure vitreuse, sans cristaux, de couleur noire (parfois verte). Elle est très dure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "894ae413-dbd1-40b7-baa6-01c820a9e3f4",
                                                "sense_id": "3b35b669-d90b-3940-a7a9-21ae09525594",
                                                "text": "Ce sont elles qui ont lancé jusqu’ici ces pierres ponces, ces obsidiennes, ces innombrables labradorites, […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da346faf-04e5-3d79-8694-50a9486c7f77",
                                        "entry_id": "fe786349-e6b8-3f65-aa6b-20276b9d9e3c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ensemble de variétés de laves (rhyolite, trachyte et andésite) ressemblant au verre, de couleur foncée (rouge, vert, noir…). Les obsidiennes sont des silicates complexes comme le feldspath ; on les appelle parfois agate d’Islande, verre des volcans"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97130302-6185-4c31-9cfe-a9ecc8222ab6",
                                                "sense_id": "da346faf-04e5-3d79-8694-50a9486c7f77",
                                                "text": "La peau d’Onawa, plus chaude qu’une obsidienne en plein soleil, était douce comme du duvet, et sucrée comme du miel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74c3e79f-382b-4052-88f4-f5db259b76ac",
                                                "sense_id": "da346faf-04e5-3d79-8694-50a9486c7f77",
                                                "text": "La jarre n'est pas loin du brasier, le jaguar - animal associé à l’inframonde pour ses habitudes crépusculaires - s'oppose à l’aigle, les pierres vertes ou la turquoise, couleur d’eau, sont la contrepartie de l’or, tout comme l’obsidienne, noire et froide, est celle du silex clair d’où jaillissent des étincelles, etc."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82088acb-31aa-4b12-944a-d3f2f2f259bb",
                                                "sense_id": "da346faf-04e5-3d79-8694-50a9486c7f77",
                                                "text": "Au Mexique les peuples aztèques fabriquèrent des outils en obsidienne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
